Three bugs surfaced junk in the Library's 'Made by Nemesis' list:
1. looksLikeArtifact's fallback (startsWith('/') && includes('.')) accepted ANY
   absolute path with a dot — leaking main.chunk.js and a malformed ':' entry.
   Replaced with a strict deliverable-extension allowlist (removes the leak).
2. Real deliverable types (.html/.docx/.pptx) were missing from FILE_EXT_RE — they
   only passed via that fallback. Added them; dropped .json/.zip/archives.
3. Dedup keyed on session.id, so one file shown once per chat. loadRecentArtifacts
   now collapses by filename (student build), newest wins.
Verified live: list went 5 junk entries → 1 real deliverable. Tests: looksLikeArtifact (3).
